# Outland Liberator cast on turn 3 makes it day at once (CR 702.145d: a game that is neither day nor night and a
# permanent with daybound on the battlefield). Bot2's turn 4 then goes by with nothing cast, so the untap step of
# turn 5 finds it day and the previous turn's active player having cast no spells, and it becomes night (CR 502.2,
# 731.2) — which turns the Liberator over into Frenzied Trapbreaker on the spot (CR 702.145c).
#
# Handed over at the attack, for picturing a board the client had never drawn: the designation is on the wire and
# the phase bar says Night, with a 3/3 back face under it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Forest
Outland Liberator
Forest x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Outland Liberator.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

# CR 702.145d, as the state-based actions are checked: no card said so and no turn had to pass.
? DayNight = Day
? Bot1.Battlefield.Outland Liberator.Power = 2

# Turn 4 is Bot2's and they cast nothing, so it is night by the time turn 5 begins — and not before: Bot1 cast a
# spell on turn 3, so the untap step of turn 4 left it day.
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? DayNight = Night
? Bot1.Battlefield.Frenzied Trapbreaker.Power = 3

[Handover Bot1.Attack]

[Expect]
Turn = 5
DayNight = Night
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Forest; Frenzied Trapbreaker
Bot1.Battlefield.Frenzied Trapbreaker.Keywords = Nightbound
